01:03:41,052 --> 01:03:47,052
Rental Family is a 2025 comedy-drama film directed by
Hikari, who co-wrote it with Stephen Blahut.

12
01:09:28,421 --> 01:09:34,421
It stars Brendan Fraser as an American actor based in Japan who begins working for a
rental family agency, where he plays roles in the lives of strangers.

13
01:15:15,789 --> 01:15:21,789
The supporting cast includes Takehiro Hira, Mari Yamamoto,
Shannon Mahina Gorman, and Akira Emoto.

14
01:21:03,157 --> 01:21:09,157
An international co-production between the United States and Japan, Rental Family premiered at the 2025 Toronto International
Film Festival on September 6 and was released in the United States by Searchlight Pictures on November 21, 2025.

15
01:26:50,526 --> 01:26:56,526
It received positive reviews from critics, who singled out Fraser's performance.

16
01:32:37,894 --> 01:32:43,894
The National Board of Review included it on its list of the year's top 10 films.

17
01:38:25,263 --> 01:38:31,263
The film explores themes of self-discovery, tokyo,
japan, expatriate, surrogate father, actor.

18
01:44:12,631 --> 01:44:18,631
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
